The Widget and ModData types are not found in the repository under the expected paths, and the base classes appear to be sealed or non-virtual, preventing subclassing or overriding. Also, the HttpClient call is non-virtual and created inside the method, so it cannot be mocked or intercepted easily.

Given these constraints, I will write a simple test that calls RefreshServerList and verifies that it sets the searchStatus field to Fetching and that it does not throw exceptions. This will provide some coverage of the method including the call to HttpClient.GetAsync, even if we cannot mock it.

I will submit a minimal test file with this approach now.

